Chapter: GopWebHold
  cites Works chapter GopWeb

 The falsifier for the holder shape. Three readings, each from a
 different process, each answering a question the others cannot:

   the service's capability word carries Network, read from the table
   after the spawn, because the word was copied at that instant;

   this process, having held Network for the spawn, is refused the NIC
   by net-status after gopweb-hold restricts it;

   a child spawned AFTER the restrict inherits the restricted word and is
   refused the same way.

 The sabotage: delete the two restricts in gopweb-hold and the second and
 third lines turn False while the first stays True. Delete Network from
 the opening's row and the first turns False.

Section: Body

  net-bit-set : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  net-bit-set (word) (bit) = bit-and word (bit-shl 1 bit) /= 0

  opening : [Console, Concurrent, Capability, Network.Read, Network.Write] Nothing = act
    blk <- gopweb-hold
    let svc = peek-32 blk gopweb-blk-pid
    in let word = process-get-cap svc
    in act
      print-line-uni ("service holds network " & show (net-bit-set word cap-network-read & net-bit-set word cap-network-write))
      mine <- net-status
      print-line-uni ("holder refused " & show (mine < 0))
      let z = poke-byte 28000 0 9
      in act
        late <- process-spawn (\x -> poke-byte 28000 0 (if net-status < 0 then 1 else 2))
        let wt = process-wait late
        in act
          print-line-uni ("late child refused " & show (peek-byte 28000 0 == 1))
          k <- process-kill svc
          print-line-uni ("service stopped " & show (k >= 0))
        end
      end
    end
  end
